# Decimal multiplication preserves operand scale

Multiplies 1.20 by 2.30 to verify the product combines the two-digit
fractional scales of its operands, producing 2.7600.

>>> source
const decimal_left: decimal = 1.20
const decimal_right: decimal = 2.30

const decimal_product: decimal = decimal_left * decimal_right
print(decimal_product)

<<< stdout
2.7600

<<< stderr
